k_m Modeling Capacity to represent system dynamics
k_l Learning Capacity to update understanding from experience
k_e Experimentation Capacity to test interventions safely
k_c Coordination Capacity to align distributed actors
k_r Rule-revision Capacity to modify institutional rules
k_g Goal-revision Capacity to reconsider objectives
k_s Structural-reconfiguration Capacity to reorganize networks and institutions
k_x Meta-transformation Capacity to modify transformation mechanisms

6.2 Capability Hierarchy

ASTF proposes a hierarchical ordering of transformation capability:

\boxed{K_0 < K_1 < K_2 < K_3 < K_4 < K_5}

Level Name Description Required Capability Components
K_0 Static No intentional adaptation to changing conditions —
K_1 Parameter Adaptation Modifies parameters while preserving rules and structures k_o, k_m
K_2 Rule Adaptation Modifies operational rules in response to feedback k_o, k_m, k_l, k_r
K_3 Structural Adaptation Reorganizes institutions, networks, or structures k_o, k_m, k_l, k_c, k_s
K_4 Goal Adaptation Reconsiders the objectives guiding transformation k_o, k_m, k_l, k_e, k_c, k_g
K_5 Meta-Adaptation Modifies the mechanisms determining how to adapt All components including k_x

This hierarchy is proposed as a testable hypothesis, not a final taxonomy.

6.3 The Capability State Space

The capability state K_t lives in a convex subset of \mathbb{R}^9:

\mathcal{K} = \{ K \in \mathbb{R}^9 : 0 \leq k_i \leq k_i^{\max} \}

Each component k_i is normalized to a comparable scale, allowing meaningful comparison across dimensions.

6.4 Distinguishing Capability as State vs. Capability as Function

A subtle distinction: K_t represents the system's current capability state, while the function \kappa represents the dynamics of capability evolution. The capability state is a point in \mathcal{K}; the capability dynamics are a mapping:

\kappa: \mathcal{K} \times \mathcal{T} \times \mathcal{L} \times \mathcal{E} \times \Theta \rightarrow \mathcal{K}

This distinction prevents confusion between the system's current capacity and the process through which that capacity changes.

