6.6 Latent Variable Measurement Model

Since K_t is a multi-dimensional latent construct, it can be estimated using a structural equation model:

K = \Lambda \eta + \varepsilon

where \Lambda is a factor loading matrix, \eta is the latent capability vector, and \varepsilon is measurement error.

6.7 Capability Dynamics

Capabilities evolve over time through learning, investment, and decay:

K_{t+1} = K_t + \Delta K_{\text{learning}} + \Delta K_{\text{investment}} + \Delta K_{\text{decay}}

where:

\Delta K_{\text{learning}} = \eta_L \, L_t

\Delta K_{\text{investment}} = \eta_I \, \mathcal{T}_K

\Delta K_{\text{decay}} = -\eta_D \, K_t

and \eta_L, \eta_I, \eta_D are positive rate parameters, \mathcal{T}_K is the portion of intervention resources allocated to capability building.

