15. The Meta-Transformation Problem

15.1 The Deepest Question

\boxed{\text{"How can a system improve the way it determines how it should change?"}}

15.2 The Finite Hierarchy Solution

To avoid infinite regression, ASTF introduces a finite hierarchy of meta-levels:

K^{(0)}_t, K^{(1)}_t, K^{(2)}_t, \ldots, K^{(L)}_t

where level l can modify level l-1. The recursion terminates at level L, which the system cannot modify.

15.3 The Parameterized Adaptation Algorithm

Let the adaptation algorithm be parameterized by \phi_t:

\mathcal{A}_t = \mathcal{A}(\cdot; \phi_t)

The meta-transformation equation becomes:

\phi_{t+1} = \omega(\phi_t, E_t, L_t)

15.4 The Bounded Recursive Structure

· Level 0: The system adapts its behavior: S_t \rightarrow S_{t+1}
· Level 1: The system adapts its adaptation rules: \phi^{(1)}_t \rightarrow \phi^{(1)}_{t+1}
· Level 2: The system adapts its rules for adapting adaptation rules: \phi^{(2)}_t \rightarrow \phi^{(2)}_{t+1}
· Level L: The system cannot modify \phi^{(L)}

The depth of this recursion, L, is itself a measure of the system's transformation capability.

