28. Conclusion

Humanity has developed powerful theories for understanding systems and practical methods for changing them. Yet the theories remain distributed across disciplines, and no single framework adequately addresses the full complexity of adaptive systemic transformation.

The Adaptive System Transformation Framework proposes that complex systems should be studied not only according to what they are, but also according to how capable they are of changing what they are.

The central formal contribution of v0.4 is the consolidation of the three-layer dynamical architecture:

\boxed{X_t = (S_t, K_t, \theta_t)}

with dynamics:

\boxed{
