K.12 The Mechanism Stability Theorem

```
+================================================================================+
|           MECHANISM STABILITY THEOREM                                         |
+================================================================================+
|                                                                                |
|   CONDITION:                                                                   |
|                                                                                |
|   For all theta_1, theta_2 in Theta and x_1, x_2 in X:                        |
|                                                                                |
|   ||g(theta_1, x_1) - g(theta_2, x_2)||                                       |
|       <= beta ||theta_1 - theta_2|| + gamma ||x_1 - x_2||                     |
|                                                                                |
|   where beta < 1 and gamma >= 0                                                |
|                                                                                |
|   +----------------------------------------------------------------+          |
|   |                    INTERPRETATION OF beta                      |          |
|   |                                                                 |          |
|   |   beta << 1 : Rapid convergence to stable mechanism             |          |
|   |   beta -> 1 : Prolonged meta-transition period                  |          |
|   |   beta > 1  : Runaway self-modification (instability)          |          |
|   +----------------------------------------------------------------+          |
|                                                                                |
|   =========================================================================    |
|                                                                                |
|   THEOREM:                                                                    |
|                                                                                |
|   If beta < 1, then for any fixed input sequence {x_t}:                       |
|                                                                                |
|   1. The iteration theta_{t+1} = g(theta_t, x_t) converges                    |
|   2. The limit is unique                                                     |
|   3. The limit depends continuously on {x_t}                                 |
|                                                                                |
|   =========================================================================    |
|                                                                                |
|   CONVERGENCE RATE:                                                           |
|                                                                                |
|   ||theta_t - theta^*|| <= (beta^t / (1-beta)) ||theta_0 - theta_0^*||        |
|                                                                                |
|   CONTINUITY:                                                                 |
|                                                                                |
|   ||theta_t^* - theta_t'^*|| <= (gamma delta / (1-beta))                      |
|                                                                                |
|   where delta = sup_t ||x_t - x_t'||                                          |
|                                                                                |
+================================================================================+
```

