K.24 The Complete Mathematical Structure

```
+================================================================================+
|           COMPLETE MATHEMATICAL STRUCTURE OF ASTF                           |
+================================================================================+
|                                                                                |
|   SPACES:                                                                     |
|                                                                                |
|   S in S          : State space (compact subset of R^n)                       |
|   K in K          : Capability space (compact subset of R^9)                  |
|   theta in Theta  : Mechanism parameter space (compact subset of R^p)         |
|   X = (S, K, theta) in P = S x K x Theta : Phase space                       |
|                                                                                |
|   FUNCTIONS:                                                                  |
|                                                                                |
|   f    : S x T x Theta -> S         : State transition                       |
|   kappa: K x T x L x E x Theta -> K : Capability update                      |
|   g    : Theta x S x A x I x L -> Theta : Mechanism update                   |
|                                                                                |
|   METRICS:                                                                    |
|                                                                                |
|   D(T)     : Transformation depth        -> [0, 1]                            |
|   TCD(T)   : Capability dividend        -> R                                  |
|   beta     : Contractivity parameter    -> [0, infinity)                      |
|   R_T(pi)  : Systemic risk              -> [0, infinity)                      |
|   C(pi)    : Transformation cost        -> [0, infinity)                      |
|                                                                                |
|   OPTIMIZATION:                                                               |
|                                                                                |
|   T* = argmax_{T in T_feasible} U(T)                                         |
|                                                                                |
|   U(T) = E[sum gamma^t r(X_t, T_t)] - lambda_R R_T(pi) - lambda_C C(pi)      |
|                                                                                |
|   CONSTRAINTS:                                                                |
|                                                                                |
|   X_t in X_acceptable (viability)                                             |
|   R_T <= R_max (risk bound)                                                   |
|   C <= C_max (cost bound)                                                     |
|   P_t governs AI actions (authority)                                          |
|                                                                                |
|   THEOREMS:                                                                   |
|                                                                                |
|   1. Banach Fixed-Point Theorem -> mechanism stability                        |
|   2. Parameterized Contraction -> continuous dependence                       |
|   3. Maximum Hamming Distance -> depth normalization                          |
|   4. Capability Convergence -> capability fixed point                         |
|   5. Positive Capability Dividend -> conditions for TCD > 0                   |
|   6. Optimal Allocation -> first-order condition for alpha                    |
|   7. Tier-Depth Monotonicity -> governance design                             |
|   8. Separation of Agency/Authority -> formal governance                     |
|                                                                                |
+================================================================================+
```

