K.25 The Transformation Operator Evolution

```
+================================================================================+
|           TRANSFORMATION OPERATOR EVOLUTION                                  |
+================================================================================+
|                                                                                |
|   +----------------------------------------------------------------+          |
|   |                    OPERATOR AT TIME t                          |          |
|   |                                                                 |          |
|   |   F_t = f(. ; theta_t)                                         |          |
|   |                                                                 |          |
|   |   theta_t = (theta_1, theta_2, ..., theta_p)                   |          |
|   |                                                                 |          |
|   |   +--------------------------------------------------+        |          |
|   |   |  MECHANISM COMPONENTS                            |        |          |
|   |   |                                                  |        |          |
|   |   |  theta_1: Observation weight                     |        |          |
|   |   |  theta_2: Model parameter                        |        |          |
|   |   |  theta_3: Intervention threshold                 |        |          |
|   |   |  theta_4: Learning rate                          |        |          |
|   |   |  theta_5: Rule revision threshold                |        |          |
|   |   |  ...                                            |        |          |
|   |   |  theta_p: Meta-adaptation parameter              |        |          |
|   |   +--------------------------------------------------+        |          |
|   +----------------------------------------------------------------+          |
|                              |                                                |
|                              v                                                |
|   +----------------------------------------------------------------+          |
|   |                    META-TRANSFORMATION                        |          |
|   |                                                                 |          |
|   |   theta_{t+1} = g(theta_t, S_t, A_t, I_t, L_t)                |          |
|   |                                                                 |          |
|   |   If g is contractive (beta < 1):                              |          |
|   |   theta_t -> theta^* (unique stable mechanism)                 |          |
|   |                                                                 |          |
|   |   If beta > 1:                                                  |          |
|   |   Potential runaway self-modification                          |          |
|   +----------------------------------------------------------------+          |
|                              |                                                |
|                              v                                                |
|   +----------------------------------------------------------------+          |
|   |                    OPERATOR AT TIME t+1                       |          |
|   |                                                                 |          |
|   |   F_{t+1} = f(. ; theta_{t+1})                                |          |
|   |                                                                 |          |
|   |   The system now transforms differently than before.           |          |
|   +----------------------------------------------------------------+          |
|                                                                                |
|   =========================================================================    |
|                                                                                |
|   KEY INSIGHT:                                                                |
|   The transformation operator is not fixed; it evolves through                |
|   meta-adaptation. This is the core novelty of ASTF.                          |
|                                                                                |
+================================================================================+
```

